$comment
LiteScope capture of litex_sim --with-analyzer, triggered on the rising edge of
simsoc_ibus_stb (litescope_cli -r simsoc_ibus_stb): 20 samples around the trigger,
two time steps per sample. doc/wiki/Use-LiteScope-To-Debug-A-SoC.md
$end
$timescale 0ps $end
$scope module top $end
$var wire 1 ! simsoc_ibus_stb $end
$var wire 1 " simsoc_ibus_cyc $end
$var wire 30 # simsoc_ibus_adr $end
$var wire 1 $ simsoc_ibus_we $end
$var wire 1 % simsoc_ibus_ack $end
$var wire 4 & simsoc_ibus_sel $end
$var wire 32 ' simsoc_ibus_dat_w $end
$var wire 32 ( simsoc_ibus_dat_r $end
$var wire 1 ) simsoc_dbus_stb $end
$var wire 1 * simsoc_dbus_cyc $end
$var wire 30 + simsoc_dbus_adr $end
$var wire 1 , simsoc_dbus_we $end
$var wire 1 - simsoc_dbus_ack $end
$var wire 4 . simsoc_dbus_sel $end
$var wire 32 / simsoc_dbus_dat_w $end
$var wire 32 0 simsoc_dbus_dat_r $end
$var wire 1 1 scope_clk $end
$var wire 1 2 scope_trig $end
$upscope $end
$enddefinitions $end
$dumpvars
b0 !
b0 "
b000000000000000001000000101000 #
b0 $
b0 %
b1111 &
b00000000000000000000000000000000 '
b00001011000000000000000001101111 (
b0 )
b0 *
b000000000000000000000000000000 +
b1 ,
b0 -
b1100 .
b00000000000000000000000000000000 /
b00001011000000000000000001101111 0
b0 1
b1 2
b0 ,
b1111 .
b00000000000000000000000110100100 /
b1 1
$end
